# =============================================================================
# MK PANEL ZONE — environment template
#
# Local development: copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# Production (Vercel): Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. This template is NOT — it is the only record of which
# variables the app actually reads. Never put a real secret in this file.
#
# Every variable below was verified by grepping `process.env.*` across `src/`,
# `prisma/` and `next.config.ts`. There is no `NEXTAUTH_URL`: this app does not
# use NextAuth. Authentication is custom and cookie-based — see
# `src/lib/ownerAuth.ts`.
# =============================================================================


# ── Database — REQUIRED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string. Vercel's Postgres integration sets both of these
# automatically; set them by hand if you bring your own database.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE

# Used by Prisma for migrations and for pooled connections — normally the direct
# (non-pooled) endpoint on the same host.
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE


# ── Owner access — REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION ────────────────────────────────────
# This is the ONLY way to sign in to the owner panel once deployed.
#
# The owner account cannot use the normal sign-in form: `managementLogin`
# deliberately refuses OWNER accounts and returns "Invalid credentials", and the
# development auth bypass in `src/lib/ownerAuth.ts` is switched off whenever
# NODE_ENV=production.
#
# To obtain an owner session, visit:
#
#     https://<your-domain>/api/mk-bootstrap?token=<OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN>
#
# That sets a 7-day httpOnly `owner_session` cookie and redirects to the panel.
# The route returns 404 for any wrong token, so it cannot be discovered.
#
# IF THIS IS UNSET IN PRODUCTION, THE OWNER PANEL IS UNREACHABLE. You would have
# to set it and redeploy. Generate a long random value, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Treat it exactly like a password — anyone holding it can become the owner.
OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=


# ── Checkout hand-off — recommended ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Receiving WhatsApp number in international format WITHOUT a leading `+`,
# e.g. 923001234567.
#
# A completed checkout sends the customer to WhatsApp with the order details
# pre-filled. If unset, the order is still recorded and shown on the success
# page, but there is no hand-off link and the customer must be contacted another
# way — `submitOrder` returns `whatsappUrl: null` in that case.
OWNER_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=


# ── Media storage — optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase Storage holds uploaded product media and payment screenshots.
#
# These are PUBLISHABLE values and are safe in the browser bundle — access is
# governed by storage bucket policies, not by secrecy. The service-role key must
# NEVER be placed here or anywhere else in this project; it would grant full
# database access to anyone who reads the bundle.
#
# Both have working fallbacks hardcoded in `src/lib/supabaseClient.ts`, so the
# app runs without them — but set your own project's values before going live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
